{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/969653-dancing-the-moonlight-lunar-3e-full-splat-homebrew-wip","id":969653,"title":"Dancing the Moonlight: Lunar 3E Full Splat Homebrew (WIP)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-14T21:51:57-07:00","id":969653,"title":"Dancing the Moonlight: Lunar 3E Full Splat Homebrew (WIP)","content":"So, I have decided that I want to create the full Lunar splat, charms and all, mainly because...<br /> <br /> A. They are my favorites...despite not having anything really that good thus far.<br /> <br /> And...that's mostly it. I know some people have tried some things so far, but they haven't really worked to my tastes so far. I did borrow a few concepts from what I've seen to compile what I felt was good so far. I noted where I borrowed things within the document.<br /> <br /> I guess some design goals first? <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The only Charm I'm porting over from past editions is Deadly Beastman Transformation. I know a lot of people like it (it was never my personal preference), so I'm dragging it over. I do want there to be other combat options though. I kind of want to start from..sort of scratch honestly.</li> <li>Each Attribute Tree will have combat tree, two utility trees, and an automatic form gain (You can now become plants) and a form gaining method (Heart's Blood or something) per tree.</li> <li>I want them to be...a step below Solars power level wise? Without just making them Solar Jr (But with animal forms!)</li> </ol><br /> Note the following. <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I am not even close to done currently. I'm almost all the way through first draft Strength Charms, and a bit into Dex...but that's about it. Any feedback on whatever is good though.</li> <li>There's going to be some holes in things as I move through this. I DO plan on going all the way. It will take some time though.</li> </ol><br /> And without further ado...here's the Link <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OUx0CSOlBT64NAFYIctGQkvYYjTz1GiZUNJJhkGp4Vg/edit\" target=\"_blank\">LUNAR LINK THING HERE</a><br /> <br /> If you have any suggestions or ideas, I'm willing to field them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":336,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","user":"MonkofLords","date":". 09-15-2016, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:59:38-07:00","id":970352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MonkofLords</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/969653-dancing-the-moonlight-lunar-3e-full-splat-homebrew-wip#post969653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]The only Charm I'm porting over from past editions is Deadly Beastman Transformation. I know a lot of people like it (it was never my personal preference), so I'm dragging it over. I do want there to be other combat options though. I kind of want to start from..sort of scratch honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Scratch </i>scratch? I ask because there are certain design goals if you're aiming for something in line with 3E's interpretation of Lunars.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts#Lunars\" target=\"_blank\">Check out this.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MonkofLords</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/969653-dancing-the-moonlight-lunar-3e-full-splat-homebrew-wip#post969653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want them to be...a step below Solars power level wise? Without just making them Solar Jr (But with animal forms!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Be careful about this. The trick is that nobody matches the raw power of the Solars. It may be better to focus on what makes them interesting, and then use &quot;but not as powerful as the Solars&quot; as a mental check you run after creating a power. For an excellent example of how to make characters who aren't as powerful as Solars, but whose coolness goes in its own direction, check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/881714-a-clutch-of-dragons-hub-thread\">Crumplepunch's excellent write-up on Dragon-Blooded.</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T18:13:18-07:00","id":970363,"title":"","content":"The Full Moon's ability to improve their resistances is a cool power, but lacks the aggressive attitude associated with this Caste. I'd suggest something which cows those who would challenge them (but you've already kinda got that).<br /> <br /> The Changing Moon's ability to assume someone's Intimacy strikes me as odd. How would that work in play?<br /> <br /> I don't get how the No Moon's ability to hide their intentions ties into their Caste. I also don't recommend having one of their three features require them to be sorcerers. Sure, they ought to have something which makes them better sorcerers than other Lunars, but it ought to be something more fundamental.<br /> <br /> Remember to include some limit on being able to assume the form of creatures with Legendary Size. A Tyrant Lizard is Essence 1, but not every Lunar is meant to have access to that out the gate.<br /> <br /> It's unclear whether you're limiting Lunars from taking form-shifting Charms without an investment. The idea in the core book is that any Lunar can assume shapes through the numerous methods (heart's blood, sex, etc.). It's just that Deadly Beastman Transformation is a Charm. That said, you might have other Form charms based on the other trees. That said, the nine you came up with are pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T18:42:46-07:00","id":970377,"title":"","content":"I've looked through the Strength Charms. I like the general feel of the combat tree, but the Charms for improving Intimacies feels more like something you'd get with &quot;Stamina&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:54:38-07:00","id":970427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Sword Emperor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/969653-dancing-the-moonlight-lunar-3e-full-splat-homebrew-wip?p=970352#post970352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Scratch </i>scratch? I ask because there are certain design goals if you're aiming for something in line with 3E's interpretation of Lunars.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts#Lunars\" target=\"_blank\">Check out this.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Be careful about this. The trick is that nobody matches the raw power of the Solars. It may be better to focus on what makes them interesting, and then use &quot;but not as powerful as the Solars&quot; as a mental check you run after creating a power. For an excellent example of how to make characters who aren't as powerful as Solars, but whose coolness goes in its own direction, check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/881714-a-clutch-of-dragons-hub-thread\">Crumplepunch's excellent write-up on Dragon-Blooded.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the goal isn't to literally make them on par. That was me misspeaking if that was the case. I want them to feel like powerful celestials. Beings a raw potential and natural might. Not necessarily &quot;Werewolf Exalts&quot; but more raw emotional and physical presence, and the potential for great change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Sword Emperor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/969653-dancing-the-moonlight-lunar-3e-full-splat-homebrew-wip?p=970363#post970363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Full Moon's ability to improve their resistances is a cool power, but lacks the aggressive attitude associated with this Caste. I'd suggest something which cows those who would challenge them (but you've already kinda got that).<br /> <br /> The Changing Moon's ability to assume someone's Intimacy strikes me as odd. How would that work in play?<br /> <br /> I don't get how the No Moon's ability to hide their intentions ties into their Caste. I also don't recommend having one of their three features require them to be sorcerers. Sure, they ought to have something which makes them better sorcerers than other Lunars, but it ought to be something more fundamental.<br /> <br /> Remember to include some limit on being able to assume the form of creatures with Legendary Size. A Tyrant Lizard is Essence 1, but not every Lunar is meant to have access to that out the gate.<br /> <br /> It's unclear whether you're limiting Lunars from taking form-shifting Charms without an investment. The idea in the core book is that any Lunar can assume shapes through the numerous methods (heart's blood, sex, etc.). It's just that Deadly Beastman Transformation is a Charm. That said, you might have other Form charms based on the other trees. That said, the nine you came up with are pretty cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea for the full moon resolve against intimidation was mostly that one does not scare off the great beast of terror! I was considering an intimidate bonus similar to what Dawns have...but I also just didn't want to copy Dawns.<br /> <br /> The changing moon ability was meant as more of a way to allow them to be mercurial, fickle and strange, by allowing them to constantly bounce around between intimacies.<br /> <br /> The No Moon ability to resist Read Intentions was more a...wise man you meet on the road thing. Basically allowing them to be inscrutable. I'm not totally on bored with the straight up sorcery boosting power either. I wanted something originally that could be directly useful with sorcery without flat out being directly tied to it, so I'm open there.<br /> <br /> And what I was thinking, at least for now, that each Attribute would have two charms you get for free if you have an Excellency in that Attribute. One Form Taking trick (Heart's Blood, Sex, etc), and one new type of form (Demons, Plants, Exceptionally Large Creatures, etc). This is in flux though<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Sword Emperor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/969653-dancing-the-moonlight-lunar-3e-full-splat-homebrew-wip?p=970377#post970377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've looked through the Strength Charms. I like the general feel of the combat tree, but the Charms for improving Intimacies feels more like something you'd get with &quot;Stamina&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That third strength tree was...tough to come up with. Given Lunars are beings of ever changing emotion, it was suggested to me to have a tree for &quot;Emotional Strength and Potential&quot;. This tree is probably going to receive more edits and changes than anything else TBH.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T23:40:57-07:00","id":977634,"title":"","content":"Well, I've made a number of updates. I changed the No Moon's first effect to a Distortion effect, and I've started to work on the...foundation charms for all the trees. I figure I'm going to work on the Essence 1 stuff to get an idea for each tree before moving on. I'm not all the way through that, but I am working on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T00:48:21-07:00","id":980147,"title":"","content":"Okay, so each tree has its foundation charms (IE Essence 1 charms with no requirements) to give each tree a basis. Next, I'll complete each tree's Essence 1 charms and move forward from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T23:01:08-07:00","id":993907,"title":"","content":"Okay, so it's been a while. Business trip slowed me down. All Essence 1 Charms are complete (First Draft that is). I drafted up really basic character creation rules, and Form Taking Tricks. Next is Essence 2 charms. Feel free to comment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T22:29:30-07:00","id":995083,"title":"","content":"Question:<br /> <br /> How do you feel about charms which replace Dex as a combat stat in some capacity? (IE Strength replaces Dex on Attack, Int replaces Dex for Parry).<br /> <br /> In my original idea, each tree had 1 combat tree, and 2 Utility. Mostly because I like symmetry and all that. But I've heard mixed opinions. Some positive, and some negative...so before I continue, I'd like to get some more feedback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T05:40:28-07:00","id":995591,"title":"","content":"3e Lunars already allow you to augment one Attribute with another appropriate one with their Excellency. I could see the case for charms which built upon that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T23:43:02-07:00","id":995982,"title":"","content":"Well, yes...now that I think about it, would it be too fiddly if charms had options for stunting in another attribute (as how the excellency works) and get different bonuses based on additional attribute stunted in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T22:00:07-07:00","id":997009,"title":"","content":"Well, I've converted Charisma, Intelligence, Manipulation, Perception, and Appearance to not have combat trees. So that cleans things up a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:43:08-08:00","id":1004641,"title":"","content":"So...I'm having some difficulty with Social Charms for Lunars, so I'm attempting to fish for ideas for Charisma, Manipulation, and Appearance, to round them out. Anyone have any?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T16:06:49-08:00","id":1004688,"title":"","content":"<b>Appearance</b><br /> The Lunar can confidently walk through any group of people, and he will not be stopped.<br /> <br /> The Lunar may convert his wound penalties into bonus dice to Intimidate others. These dice count as non-Charm dice if the intimidate attempt is flurried with an attack action.<br /> <br /> It is impossible to prevaricate before a Lunar's majesty. Anyone speaking with the Lunar - whose Resolve is lower than the Lunar's appearance - must speak the truth to them, and cannot lie by omission or intentional misunderstanding, nor can they attempt to leave the Lunar's presence so long as there is more to be revealed. Effects may be mitigated with the expenditure of Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Manipulation</b><br /> It is simply impossible to question the wisdom of the Chosen. If a Lunar makes a statement, listeners will not question its factual basis and will actually resist anyone who attempts to convince them to look into the Lunar's statements.<br /> <br /> Through sheer force of willpower, the Lunar may affect the way others speak. At the end of a conversation or speech, the Lunar may activate this Charm to force the listener to adopt some colloquialism or turn of phrase into their standard vocabulary. They will be unaware that their manner of speech has changed unless someone draws attention to it, and even then will believe they have always spoken this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T18:24:26-08:00","id":1005180,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, anyone have any idea about Charisma charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T22:53:19-08:00","id":1011871,"title":"","content":"An update, I am through Essence 2 of Social Charms, moving on to Essence 2 Mental Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T21:45:26-08:00","id":1036436,"title":"","content":"It's been a while. But, after a break during the Holidays, all Essence 2 charms are done...next onto Essence 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}